  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Connectivity and Sustainability in Bihar Roads Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bihar is the 12th largest state in India by area, covering about 99,000 square kilometers (km2); the third most populous, with about 104 million inhabitants; and the sixth most densely populated. It is in the eastern region of the country, bordering Uttar Pradesh in the west, West Bengal in the east, and Jharkhand in the south. The Ganga River flows through the middle of the Bihar plain from west to east, physically dividing the state into northern and southern regions. The northern region is bordered by Nepal.</narrative>
  </description>
